# Frontend Stack Rule

Apply this rule for application code changes in this repository.

## Stack Assumptions

- React 19, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind v3.
- Prefer guidance compatible with this stack.
- Do not assume Next.js-only primitives unless explicitly requested.

## Coding Standards

- Keep types explicit for public APIs and complex state.
- Favor small composable components and hooks.
- Prefer predictable state flow and clear side-effect boundaries.
- Follow existing project patterns before introducing new abstractions.

## Tailwind / UI Standards

- Reuse existing utility patterns and shared components.
- Keep class usage consistent and avoid one-off style drift.
- Do not apply Tailwind v4-specific migration advice by default.
